# Cyber Security Internship - Task 4

## Title
Setup and Use a Firewall on Windows

## Objective
To configure and inspect a firewall rule to block inbound traffic on TCP port 23.

## Tools Used
- Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security
- Windows laptop

## Procedure
1. Opened Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security.
2. Checked the existing inbound rules.
3. Created a rule to block inbound TCP traffic on port 23.
4. Inspected the rule settings.
5. Removed the temporary test rule after documenting it.

## Result
Record whether the rule was created successfully and whether traffic blocking was independently tested.

## Real-Life Applications
- Protecting computers from unwanted network connections.
- Monitoring and managing network traffic.
- Supporting SOC analysis and network security.
- Reviewing firewall settings during authorized security assessments.

